        <name>syn_hpclock_ticks_to_ns</name>
        <param>
          <type>uint64_t</type>
          <declname>ticks</declname>
        </param>
        <briefdescription>
<para>Convert a tick count to nanoseconds. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>Uses integer-only arithmetic: ns = ticks * 1000000000 / freq_hz. The division is performed with 64-bit precision to avoid overflow.</para>
<para><parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>ticks</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Tick count from <ref refid="syn__hpclock_8h_1a718cf3f25a151f6ce2f2688593722e3b" kindref="member">syn_hpclock_resolve()</ref>. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<simplesect kind="return"><para>Equivalent time in nanoseconds. </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
        </detaileddescription>
